  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support for the Well-Being of Crisis-Affected Populations in the Far North of Cameroon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Far North region of Cameroon, which borders Nigeria and Chad, has consistently faced significant vulnerabilities due to climatic challenges and ongoing security crises. This project aims to enhance the living conditions and overall well-being of populations affected by these crises in the Far North. The International Organization for Migration (IOM) is committed to addressing the immediate and short-term needs of vulnerable communities impacted by both the humanitarian crisis and inter-community conflicts. IOM is providing reliable, actionable data to inform targeted humanitarian interventions, focusing on life-saving water, sanitation and hygiene activities.</narrative>
  </description>
